* BAP64-02 series PIN diode model for the hybrid antenna switch cell.
*
* Datasheet-anchored ngspice diode model (Nexperia BAP64-02, SOD523), NOT a
* vendor macromodel. The switch cell forward biases the two series diodes to
* connect the selected antenna and reverse biases the 63 deselected cells so
* their sub-pF junction capacitance does not detune the shared RFO bus.
*
* WHY THE .ac LINEARIZATION IS THE RF BEHAVIOUR
*   At 13.56 MHz the carrier lifetime of a PIN diode is far longer than one RF
*   period, so a forward biased diode does not rectify: it is a linear resistor
*   whose value is set by the DC bias current. ngspice computes the DC operating
*   point, then linearises the junction for .ac. With the bias network setting
*   the operating point, that linearisation reproduces the datasheet RF terminal
*   values with no behavioural stand-in:
*     rd = RS + N*Vt/IF   (forward small-signal series resistance)
*     Cd = CJO/(1+VR/VJ)^M (reverse junction capacitance)
*
* TT=0 IS DELIBERATE
*   A real transit time would add a large forward diffusion capacitance
*   (TT*gd), which at 13.56 MHz would shunt the junction and wrongly collapse
*   the forward device to a near short. Setting TT=0 keeps the forward device
*   the bias-set resistor a PIN diode actually presents at HF. This model is
*   therefore valid for small-signal .ac at the switch bias points only, not for
*   large-signal reverse-recovery or transient work.
*
* Datasheet anchor points reproduced by this model (verified in ngspice .ac):
*   IF = 10 mA  -> rd = 3.09 ohm   (datasheet ~3 ohm)
*   IF = 20 mA  -> rd = 1.79 ohm
*   VR = 1 V    -> Cd = 0.350 pF   (datasheet 0.35 pF)
*   VR = 20 V   -> Cd = 0.230 pF   (datasheet 0.23 pF)
*   N and RS reproduce the resistance bracket; CJO/VJ/M reproduce the weak
*   capacitance-versus-reverse-voltage grading. IS only sets the forward voltage
*   drop (~0.7 V at 10 mA) and does not affect the small-signal resistance.
*
* A D card references this .model name directly, so no .SUBCKT wrapper is needed
* (unlike the VDMOS switch models, which wrap an M device).
.model BAP64_02 D(IS=1e-14 N=1 RS=0.5 CJO=0.411p VJ=0.6 M=0.164 TT=0)
